@5000 = ~IA rebalancing~
@5001 = ~Rework summoning limit to not block casting spells like Wish if you have reached summon limit~
@5002 = ~Rework weapon style bonuses, improve sword and shield, 2h weapon and single weapon styles~
@5003 = ~SWORD AND SHIELD: Anyone can pick up a shield and get its basic protection bonuses, but by spending slots on this fighting style, an adventurer can maximize the benefits received.

Proficient (1 slot): The wielder gets a -1 bonus to AC and additional -1 against missile weapons.

Specialized (2 slots): The wielder gets a -2 bonus to AC and additional -2 against missile weapons.

Master (3 slots): The wielder gets a -3 bonus to AC and additional -3 against missile weapons.

NOTE: Despite the name of this style, any one-handed melee weapon in combination with a shield will receive the aforementioned bonuses.~

@5004 = ~SINGLE-WEAPON: This fighting style is for characters who do not wish to use a shield but want some bonus when using a one-handed melee weapon.

Proficient (1 slot): The wielder gets a +1 bonus to their thac0 and damage rolls, -1 bonus to AC, -1 bonus to Speed Factor and inflicts critical damage on an attack roll of 19 or 20.

Specialized (2 slots): The wielder gets a +2 bonus to their thac0 and damage, -2 bonus to AC, -2 bonus to Speed Factor and inflicts critical damage on an attack roll of 18, 19 or 20.~

@5005 = ~TWO-HANDED: This fighting style allows the character to use a two-handed melee weapon and receive special bonuses.

Proficient (1 slot): The wielder gets a +1 bonus to damage rolls, a -2 bonus to Speed Factor, and the ability to score critical hits on a roll of 19 or 20 (instead of just 20) when using a two-handed weapon.

Specialized (2 slots): The wielder gets a further +2 to damage rolls and a -2 bonus to Speed Factor.

NOTE: Magical two-handed weapons are more powerful than their single-handed counterparts. This counterbalances the fact that you can't use a second weapon or shield when using a two-handed weapon. The Holy Avenger and Vorpal Sword are examples of weapons that are two-handed.~

@5006 = ~CLERIC: The Cleric is a generic priest (of any mythos) who tends to the spiritual needs of a community. Though <PRO_HESHE> is both protector and healer, <PRO_HESHE> is not purely defensive—when evil threatens, the Cleric is well suited to seek it out on its own ground and destroy it. The opposite is true of evil Clerics as well, and there are also many variations in between.

CLASS FEATURES:

– May wear helmets.
– May wear any armor.
– May only use blunt weapons (war hammer, club, flail, mace, quarterstaff, sling) and daggers.
– May only become Proficient (one slot) in any weapon class.
– May become Specialized (two slots) in Sword and Shield fighting style.
– May only become Proficient (one slot) in any other fighting style.
– May Turn Undead.
– May cast priest spells.
– Hit Die: d8

Prime Requisites For Dual-Classing: Wisdom~

@5007 = ~Rebalance Clerics and their kits~

@5008 = ~Rebalance specialist Mage kits~

@5009 = ~Base ~ // Used to inform players that the value of Thieving Abilities they see during character creation does not include dex or race bonuses: "Base Hide in Shadows" etc.

@5010 = ~QUARTERSTAFF: A simple weapon, but in the hands of a skilled warrior, whether Mage or Paladin, the quarterstaff can lay flat any foe. Although everyone, even Thieves can use staves, they are cumbersome to use and are not suitable for backstabbing enemies.

<DOTS1>

<DOTS2>

<DOTS3>

<DOTS4>

<DOTS5>~

@5011 = ~Stealth Strike~

@5012 = ~PICK POCKETS: The rogue uses this ability when filching small items from other people's pockets, sleeves, girdles, packs, and so on. With greater skill, a talented rogue can even snatch larger items, including weapons and certain articles of clothing.

This skill requires not only nimble fingers but also keen observational abilities. True masters of pickpocketing can anticipate their target's movements, ensuring they aren't caught red-handed when the target suddenly turns around. This skill can also be used offensively, allowing rogues to identify weak points in an enemy's defenses, and defensively, enabling them to evade the trajectory of an enemy's sword.

-Each 50 points invested in pickpocketing increases rogue's AC vs melee attacks by 1 while he's wearing light armor or no armor at all.
-Each 100 points invested in pickpocketing increases rogue's AC vs melee attacks by 1 while he's wearing heavier armors.
-Each 25 points invested in pickpocketing increases the THAC0 of each first successful melee attack per round by 1.
-When above 100 points, each additional 25 points increase the chance of a critical hit on each first successful melee attack per round by 1.
-When above 200 points, each additional 12.5 points (rounded up) increase the chance of a critical hit on each first successful melee attack per round by 1."~

@5013 = ~HIDE IN SHADOWS: Using this ability, a character can disappear into shadows or any other type of concealment—bushes, curtains, crannies, etc.

A Thief who dedicates themselves to mastering the Hide in Shadows skill can achieve results that seem almost magical. With enough training, they can blend seamlessly into the darkness, moving unseen and unheard. Perhaps Shar, the Mistress of the Night, truly does favor those who walk the path of shadows, granting them the ability to vanish from sight with ease.

-The rogue might attempt to Hide in Shadows once per round
-Each 5 points give the user 5% chance to hide when no enemies are around up to 100% when the rogue reaches 100 points.
-When above 50 points, each 10 points put into this skill give 5% chance to hide when a single enemy is around, hiding around a larger group of enemies is harder, though at 250 points there is 100% chance for success.
-When above 100 points, each 10 points put into this skill lowers the time needed to use this ability by 0,1s.
-When above 200 points, the previous bonus is applied for every 5 points instead of 10.~

@5014 = ~STEALTH STRIKE: This ability allows a rogue to unleash devastating attacks from the shadows, catching their enemies completely off guard. Striking with precision and force, the rogue can deal significantly increased damage to their unsuspecting foes.

The bonuses this skill grants are only applied when the rogue succeeds at hiding in shadows.

-Up till 100 points invested, each 12,5 points invested (rounded up) grant +1 melee damage bonus that is multipied by backstab.
-When above 100 points, each 10 points invested grant +1 melee damage
-When above 200 points, each 8 points invested grant +1 melee damage.~

@5015 = ~DETECT ILLUSION: While an adventurer searches for traps, <PRO_HISHER> well-trained eyes also allow <PRO_HIMHER> to detect the minor inconsistencies caused by illusion spells. This skill is the percentage chance per round of dispelling a nonfriendly illusion spell within 30 ft.

At high skill levels, the user's vision becomes so sharp that they can perceive the flow of magic and the movements of the Weave, allowing them to evade danger or at least reduce the impact of incoming spells.

-Each point gives the user 1% chance to dispel the illusions while consciously using this ability.
-When above 100 points the rogue gets a chance to passively dispel any illusion even when not using the ability, each 10 points increase this chance by 5% up to 100% at 300 points.
-When above 100 points, each 50 points put into this skill increase the character's saving throws by 1.
-When above 100 points, each 20 points put into this skill increase the character's magic resistance by 3%.
-When above 200 points the previous bonus is improved, granting additional 3% magic resistance for every 10 points invested.~

@5016 = ~FIND TRAPS: A character uses this ability to find small traps, pit traps, and alarms. It does not find large mechanical traps. Thieves may also use this ability to disarm any traps they find.

This ability increases thieves' knowledge on mechanisms and tools used to create and set traps, enabling them to apply more sophisticated designs in their own traps.

-Each point increases the rogue's chance to spot traps and to disarm them.
-When above 100 points, each 20 points invested in this skill make the traps set by the thief operate 1 second longer before breaking.
-When above 200 points, each 10 points invested in this skill make the traps set by the thief operate 1 second longer before breaking.~

@5017 = ~SET TRAPS: A Thief's skill in disarming traps allows <PRO_HIMHER> to create snares of <PRO_HISHER> own

At higher levels the mechanisms used in traps become more precise and deadly, dealing more damage and making it harder to avoid them.

-Each 5 points five the user 5% chance to successfully set any trap, when the thief reaches 100 points in this skill he has 100% chance of success.
-When above 100 points, each 5 points invested in this skill makes all traps deal 5% more damage.
-When abobe 200 points, each 5 points invested in this skill make the traps deal 10% more damage.~

@5018 = ~PRIEST OF LATHANDER: Lathander is the good god of renewal, creativity, and youth, and is celebrated nearly everywhere. His followers are very popular throughout the realms, and there are numerous wealthy temples devoted to him.

Advantages:
- From level 20, Armor of Faith cast by this kit will grant 15% resistances, last for 50% longer and will be undispellable.
– May cast a special version of Hold Undead once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 5 levels thereafter.
- Draw Upon Holy Might cast by Priest of Lathander lasts for 15 rounds and is undispellable.
- Additional fifth level spell: Protective Chant.
- Additional sixth level spell: Life Link.
- Additional seventh level spell: Spare the Dying.
– May cast Boon of Lathander once per day. Gains one use at level 10 and another use every 6 levels thereafter.

BOON OF LATHANDER: This spell lasts for 1 turn. It gives the caster a +1 bonus to all Saving Throws, +2 to damage and thac0, and +1 extra attack per round.

- From level 15 can use Aegis of Faith ability.

AEGIS OF FAITH: Through prayer and devotion, the cleric grants themselves a protective blessing that safeguards their magical defenses. For the next turn, any effects that targets and removes specific protections will be nullified. This spell does not protect against spells and effects that dispel all types of effects at once, like Remove Magic or Purge Magic.

This blessing cannot be dispelled and remains active for its full duration.
Disadvantages:
– Alignment restricted to lawful good, neutral good, chaotic good, and true neutral.~

@5019 = ~PRIEST OF TALOS: Talos is the evil god of storms, destruction, and rebellion. Clerics of the Stormlord warn that Talos must be appeased or he will rain destruction upon the land.

Advantages:
- From level 20, Armor of Faith cast by this kit will grant 15% resistances, last for 50% longer and will be undispellable.
– May cast Lightning Bolt of Talos once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 5 levels thereafter.
- Gains early access to a HLA Purify Aura, may cast it once at level 5, then gains additional uses at levels 15, 25 and 35.
- Additional fifth level spell: Protective Chant.
- Additional sixth level spell: Life Link.
- Additional seventh level spells: Spare the Dying, Spiritual Link.
– May cast Storm Shield once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 10 levels thereafter.

STORM SHIELD: This spell lasts 1 round per level of the caster. It protects the caster from lightning, fire, cold, and normal missiles.

- From level 15 can use Aegis of Faith ability.

AEGIS OF FAITH: Through prayer and devotion, the cleric grants themselves a protective blessing that safeguards their magical defenses. For the next turn, any effects that targets and removes specific protections will be nullified. This spell does not protect against spells and effects that dispel all types of effects at once, like Remove Magic or Purge Magic.

Disadvantages:
– Alignment restricted to neutral evil, chaotic evil, and chaotic neutral.~

@5020 = ~PRIEST OF HELM: Followers of the neutral god of watchers and protectors are warriors in their own right and are often seen as defenders of the innocent.

Advantages:
- From level 20, Armor of Faith cast by this kit will grant 15% resistances, last for 50% longer and will be undispellable.
– May cast True Sight once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 5 levels thereafter.
- Is immune to Blindness effect.
- Gains one point in Long Swords at level 1.
- Additional fifth level spell: Protective Chant.
- Additional sixth level spell: Life Link.
- Additional seventh level spell: Spare the Dying.
– May cast Seeking Sword once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 10 levels thereafter.

SEEKING SWORD: This spell creates a long sword in the Cleric's inventory that only Priests of Helm can use, it stays in <PRO_HISHER> equipment for 1 round per level, up to 20 rounds. The sword can only be used in main hand and to wield the weapon better, the caster must know how to use Long Swords. The sword gets more powerful as the caster gains experience. While the sword is held — and for 2 rounds after it is removed — the Cleric's spellcasting is hampered, reducing the potency of any divine spells cast during that time.

The sword has the following statistics based on levels:
1 - 9: 1-6 + 2 dmg, +2 thaco, 1 APR, priest caster level -1
10-11: 1-6 + 2 dmg, +2 thaco, 1,5 APR, priest caster level -2
12-14: 1-8 + 3 dmg, +3 thaco, 1,5 APR, priest caster level -2
15-19: 1-8 + 3 dmg, +3 thaco, 2 APR, priest caster level -3, range increased to 2 feet
20-24: 2-4 + 4 dmg, +4 thaco, 2 APR, priest caster level -4, range increased to 2 feet, +5% chance for critical hit
25-40: 2-6 + 5 dmg, +5 thaco, 2 APR, priest caster level -5, range increased to 2 feet, +10% chance for critical hit.

- From level 15 can use Aegis of Faith ability.

AEGIS OF FAITH: Through prayer and devotion, the cleric grants themselves a protective blessing that safeguards their magical defenses. For the next turn, any effects that targets and removes specific protections will be nullified. This spell does not protect against spells and effects that dispel all types of effects at once, like Remove Magic or Purge Magic.

Disadvantages:
– Alignment restricted to lawful good, lawful neutral, lawful evil, and true neutral.~

@5021 = ~PRIEST OF TYR: Tyr is the deity of law and justice and is primarily concerned with the punishment of wrongdoers and the general furthering of law and good in the world. The belief in justice through (benevolent) force, or at least armed vigilance, is the reason for Tyr's existence. Tyr holds great prominence in the pantheon due to his position as leader of the Triad, a trio of lawful good gods that are collectively devoted to the concepts of courage, justice, perseverance, relief of suffering, duty, obedience, honor, and to some extent, righteous martyrdom.

Advantages:
- From level 20, Armor of Faith cast by this kit will grant 15% resistances, last for 50% longer and will be undispellable.
- May become Master at Sword and Shield style.
- Righteous Magic cast by Priest of Tyr becomes undispellable and lasts for 50% longer.
- Additional fifth level spell: Protective Chant.
- Additional sixth level spell: Life Link.
- Additional seventh level spell: Spare the Dying.
- Can pick Critical Strike High Level Ability up to 3 times.
– May cast Exaltation once per day every 5 levels of the caster (starts at 1st level with one use).

EXALTATION: This spell enables a priest to aid and protect any one being other than themselves. By touch, the caster removes the effects of fear, sleep, feeblemind, unconsciousness, and intoxication, as well as berserk and confused states of mind. In addition, the recipient is protected against spells and other attacks that cause these effects for 1 turn.

– May cast Divine Favor once per day every 10 levels of the caster (starts at 1st level with one use).

DIVINE FAVOR: This spell grants the caster a +1 bonus to hit and damage rolls every 3 levels of the caster, capped at +6. The spell lasts for 6 rounds.

- From level 15 can use Aegis of Faith ability.

AEGIS OF FAITH: Through prayer and devotion, the cleric grants themselves a protective blessing that safeguards their magical defenses. For the next turn, any effects that targets and removes specific protections will be nullified. This spell does not protect against spells and effects that dispel all types of effects at once, like Remove Magic or Purge Magic.

Disadvantages:
– Alignment restricted to lawful good, neutral good, or lawful neutral.~

@5022 = ~PRIEST OF TEMPUS: Tempus, also known as the Lord of Battles or the Foehammer, is random in his favors, yet his chaotic nature favors all sides equally. Lord Tempus may be on an army's side one day and against them the next; such is the nature of war. Tempuran clergy can be found on both sides of a conflict, as none can ever truly know whom the war god will favor.

Advantages:
- From level 20, Armor of Faith cast by this kit will grant 15% resistances, last for 50% longer and will be undispellable.
- Holy Power cast by Priest of Tempus lasts for 50% longer, gives additional 1/2 APR at level 12 and 1 APR from level 20, additionally it becomes undispellable.
- Additional fifth level spell: Protective Chant.
- Additional sixth level spell: Life Link.
- Additional seventh level spell: Spare the Dying.
- May cast Chaos of Battle once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 10 levels thereafter.
- Champion's Might's periodic pulses can affect up to two nearest characters at the same time.

CHAOS OF BATTLE:
This spell ensures that the next strike from all affected allies will be a critical hit, while the next strike from all affected enemies will be a critical miss. The spell lasts for 1 round. If a creature does not attack during this period, the spell's effect will be wasted on that target.

The area of effect of this spell grows with the caster's level as follows:
At levels 5-10, it affects all creatures within a 5-foot radius.
At levels 11-15, the area is increased to a 10-foot radius.
From level 16 onward, the area is increased to a 15-foot radius.

- From level 15 can use Aegis of Faith ability.

AEGIS OF FAITH: Through prayer and devotion, the cleric grants themselves a protective blessing that safeguards their magical defenses. For the next turn, any effects that targets and removes specific protections will be nullified. This spell does not protect against spells and effects that dispel all types of effects at once, like Remove Magic or Purge Magic.

Disadvantages:
– Alignment restricted to chaotic good, chaotic neutral, chaotic evil, or true neutral.~

@5023 = ~PRIEST OF TALOS: Talos is the evil god of storms, destruction, and rebellion. Clerics of the Stormlord warn that Talos must be appeased or he will rain destruction upon the land.

Advantages:
– May cast Lightning Bolt of Talos once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 5 levels thereafter.
- Gains early access to a HLA Purify Aura, may cast it once at level 5, then gains additional uses at levels 15, 25 and 35.
- Additional fifth level spell: Protective Chant.
- Additional sixth level spell: Life Link.
- Additional seventh level spells: Spare the Dying, Spiritual Link.
– May cast Storm Shield once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 10 levels thereafter.

STORM SHIELD: This spell lasts 1 round per level of the caster. It protects the caster from normal missiles and sets his lightning, fire and cold resistances to 75%.

- From level 15 can use Aegis of Faith ability.

AEGIS OF FAITH: Through prayer and devotion, the cleric grants themselves a protective blessing that safeguards their magical defenses. For the next turn, any effects that targets and removes specific protections will be nullified. This spell does not protect against spells and effects that dispel all types of effects at once, like Remove Magic or Purge Magic.

Disadvantages:
– Alignment restricted to neutral evil, chaotic evil, and chaotic neutral.~

@5024 = ~THIEF: To accomplish <PRO_HISHER> goals, for good or ill, the Thief is a skilled pilferer. Cunning, nimbleness, and stealth are <PRO_HISHER> hallmarks. Whether <PRO_HESHE> turns <PRO_HISHER> talent against innocent passersby and wealthy merchants or oppressors and monsters is a choice for the Thief to make.

CLASS FEATURES:

– May not wear armor heavier than studded leather.
– May not equip shields larger than bucklers.
– May only use the following weapons: long sword, short sword, katana, scimitar, dagger, club, quarterstaff, crossbow, shortbow, dart, sling.
– May only become Proficient (one slot) in any weapon class.
– May only become Proficient (one slot) in any fighting style.
– May distribute 10 points per level (40 at level 1) in thieving abilities: Open Locks, Pick Pockets, Find Traps, Stealth Strike, Hide In Shadows, Detect Illusion, Set Traps.
- May put up to 100 points into any Thieving Ability and up to 150 into Pick Pockets.
– Starts with base scores of 40% in Open Locks, Find Traps and Pick Pockets.
– May backstab for 2x damage.
– May use the Set Snare ability once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 5 levels thereafter.

SET SNARE: Set a trap in the chosen location when no hostile creatures are in sight. Traps grow more powerful with the Thief's level and can only be triggered by enemies.
  1st level: Deals 2d8+5 missile damage.
  11th level: Deals 2d8+5 missile damage and additionally deals 2d6 poison damage per round for the next 3 rounds.
  16th level: Deals 3d8+5 missile damage and 4d8+2 fire damage.
  21st level: Deals 3d8+5 missile damage and 20 poison damage with no save; slays target if a Save vs. Death with a +4 bonus is failed.

– Alignment restricted to any except lawful good.
– Hit Die: d6

Prime Requisites For Dual-Classing: Dexterity~

@5025 = ~ASSASSIN: This is a killer trained in discreet and efficient murder, relying on anonymity and surprise to perform his task.

Advantages:
- May coat his weapon in poison once per day per 4 levels. The next hit with that weapon will inject the poison into the target, dealing out 2 damage per second for 12 seconds. A saving throw vs. poison limits damage to 12 total. The weapon will remain poisoned for 3 rounds.
- Bonus +1 to hit and +1 damage.
- Starts with base score of 40% in Stealth Strike and Hide in Shadows.
- May put up to 200 points into Stealth Strike and Hide in Shadows.
- May become Specialized (two slots) in Short Sword, Dagger and Single Weapon Style.

Disadvantages:
- Only 10 points to distribute at level 1.
- May put only 100 points into Pick Pockets, 75 points into Find Traps and only 50 points into Detect Illusions.
- Does not get standard Thief bonuses to Open Locks, Find Traps and Pick Pockets.~

@5026 = ~BOUNTY HUNTER: This is a hunter of men, skilled in tracking quarry and bringing them back alive—whether for lawful authorities or underworld masters. Bounty Hunters are specially trained at their task and make fearsome opponents. They have honed their trap-making abilities well beyond that of the average Thief.

Advantages:
– +40% bonus to Find Traps and Set Traps.
- May put up to 200 points into Find Traps and Set Traps.
– May use the Set Special Snare ability once per day in addition to the normal Thief's Set Snare. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 5 levels thereafter.

SET SPECIAL SNARE: Set a trap in the chosen location when no hostile creatures are in sight. Traps grow more powerful with the Bounty Hunter's level and can only be triggered by enemies.
  1st level: Deals 3d8+5 missile damage and slows target for 5 rounds if a Save vs. Spell with a -4 penalty is failed.
  11th level: Deals 4d8+5 missile damage and holds target for 5 rounds if a Save vs. Spell with a -1 penalty is failed.
  16th level: Erects an Otiluke's Resilient Sphere around the target for 7 rounds if a Save vs. Spell is failed.
  21st level: Mazes the target.

Disadvantages:
- Only 10 points to distribute at level 1.
- May put only 75 points into Pick Pockets and Stealth Strike.
- Does not get standard Thief bonuses to Open Locks and Pick Pockets.~

@5027 = ~SWASHBUCKLER: This rogue is part acrobat, part swordsman and part wit: the epitome of charm and grace.

Advantages:
- Bonus +1 to AC.
- Gains +2 bonus to armor class every 9 levels.
- Gains +1 to hit and +2 to damage every 9 levels.
- Can specialize in any melee weapon that a thief can use.
- May place 3 slots into the proficiency 'two weapon fighting style'.
- At level 14 and above, every successful melee hit will have a 10% chance to apply a random effect picked from the following pool: "Mirrored Blade" (+3 AC bonus vs. all weapon types and 5% Magic Resistance for 6 rounds with unlimited stacking), "Life Pick" (heals the swashbuckler for 15 hp).
- At level 20 and above, every successful melee hit will also have 10% chance to apply a random effect picked from the following pool: "Bloodlet" (4D10 additional Piercing damage), "Maim Target" (4D10 additional crushing damage).
– Starts with base scores of 40% in Open Locks and Pick Pockets.

Disadvantages:
- No backstab multiplier.
- Only 20 points to distribute at level 1.
- May not use Set Snare ability.
- May not invest any points into Set Traps and Stealth Strike.
- Does not get standard Thief bonuses to Find Traps.~

@5028 = ~SHADOWDANCER: Shadowdancers can harness the power of magic to increase their stealth abilities. Enigmatic and dangerous, these uniquely skilled Thieves are able to blend seamlessly into the shadows in ways that a normal Thief cannot, striking without warning—sometimes with supernatural speed.

Advantages:
– +40% bonus to Hide In Shadows and Detect Illusions.
– May cast Shadowstep once per day. Gains one use at level 5 and an additional use every 5 levels thereafter.

SHADOWSTEP: Step into the Shadow Plane and move for 7 seconds while others are frozen in time. The Shadowdancer cannot attack or cast spells while in the Shadow Plane.

– Slippery Mind: +1 bonus to Saving Throws.

Disadvantages:
– Alignment restricted to any non-lawful.
- Only 10 points to distribute at level 1.
- May put only 100 points into Pick Pockets.
- Does not get standard Thief bonuses to Open Locks, Find Traps and Pick Pockets.
– May not use the Set Snare ability.
- May not invest any points into Set Traps.

Prime Requisites For Dual-Classing: Strength, Dexterity, Charisma~

@5029 = ~BEAST MASTER: This Ranger is a wanderer and is not comfortable in civilized lands. Therefore, <PRO_HESHE> maintains a natural affinity for animals; they are <PRO_HISHER> friends and comrades-in-arms, and the Beast Master has a limited form of telepathic communication with them.

Advantages:
– Can reach Mastery (three slots) in all weapons that he can use.
– Can use Hunter's Mark ability unlimited number of times.
– Gains access to two additional spells, a 2nd level spell Animal Fortitude and a 3rd level spell Animal Rage.
– Can cast a special version of Animal Summoning I, which lasts for 15 rounds and can be cast unlimited number of times, but only once per 15 rounds.
– At levels 10, 12 and 14 gains analogous versions of Animal Summoning II, III and IV respectively.
- Can pick Animal Summoning V as a HLA.
- At level 10, gains one use of the Unified Minds ability. Gains an additional use of this skill for every 10 levels thereafter.

Disadvantages:
– May only use simple non-bladed weapons.
– May not wear armor heavier than studded leather.
- Cannot dual class.

HUNTER'S MARK:
When using this ability, the Beast Master places a mystical mark on a single enemy. For the next 15 rounds the marked enemy suffers a -2 penalty to their THAC0 and damage against the Beast Master and any animals. The Beast Master and all animals within a 15-foot radius gain a +2 bonus to their damage and THAC0 against the marked enemy. Additionally, all attacks from affected animals against that target will be treated as if made with a +4 weapon for determining if the target can be damaged. All thac0 and damage bonuses/penalties increase by 1 for every 5 levels of the caster.

The Beast Master can use this ability again after 15 rounds or if the target dies.

UNIFIED MINDS:
By using this ability, the Beast Master opens his mind to one animal, allowing their senses and thoughts to bond almost as if they were a single organism. For the next turn, whenever the Beast Master and the targeted animal stand within 10 feet from each other, they can protect each other. This includes things like blocking an attack directed at one of them, alerting each other of an incoming arrow, or redirecting a hit targeted at a vital point. This ability grants a -5 bonus to AC and +10% damage reduction against all weapon types. Additionally, their connected minds protect each other from mental manipulation, granting both the Beast Master and the animal a +3 bonus to saving throws against enchantment spells. The effects from multiple uses of this ability are not cumulative. If either the Beast Master or the target animal become feared, held, charmed, disabled in any other way or stand more than 10ft away from each other, the effects of this spell will be nullified.~

@5030 = ~MONK: Monks are warriors who pursue perfection through contemplation as well as action. They are versatile fighters, especially skilled in combat without weapons or armor. Though Monks cannot cast spells, they have a unique magic of their own: they channel a subtle energy, called ki, which allows them to perform amazing feats. The Monk's best known feat is their ability to stun an opponent with an unarmed blow.

CLASS FEATURES:

- May not wear any armor.
- May only use weapons available to the Thief class (except two-handed).
- May only become Proficient (one slot) in any weapon class.
- May only become Proficient (one slot) in Single-Weapon Style and may not put slots into any other style.
- Moves 2 points faster than other characters. Movement rate further improves by 1 every 5 levels.
- May make 1 unarmed attack per round. An additional 1/2 attack per round is gained every 3 levels. Damage dealt by unarmed attacks increases with level as follows:
  Level 1-2: 1d6
  Level 3-5: 1d8
  Level 6-8: 1d10
  Level 9-14: 2d6
  Level 15-20: 2d8
  Level 21-28: 2d10
  Level 29+: 3d8
- At level 6, unarmed attacks are treated as a +1 magical weapon and gain a +1 bonus to hit and damage rolls. This enchantment improves to +2 at level 9, +3 at level 12, +4 at level 18, and +5 at level 25.
- Receives a +2 bonus to Saving Throws vs. Spell.
- Deflect Missiles: +1 bonus to AC vs. missile attacks every 3 levels.
- Starts with an Armor Class of 9 at 1st level and gains an additional +1 bonus every 2 levels.
- May use the Stunning Blow ability once per day. Gains one use at level 1 and an additional use every 4 levels thereafter.
- May use the Flurry of Blows ability once per day. Gains one use at level 11, 16 and 21.
- May use the Diamond Body ability once per day. Gains one use at levels 17, 22 and 27.
- 5th level: Becomes immune to all diseases and cannot be slowed or hasted.
- 7th level: May use the Lay On Hands ability on <PRO_HIMHER>self to heal 2 Hit Points per level.
- 8th level: Gains a -1 bonus to Speed Factor.
- 9th level: Gains a +1 bonus to all Saving Throws and becomes immune to charm.
- 11th level: Becomes immune to poison.
- 12th level: Gains another -1 bonus to Speed Factor.
- 13th level: May use the Quivering Palm ability once per day.
- 14th level: Gains 3% Magic Resistance per level (starting with 42% at 14th level).
- 20th level: Becomes immune to non-magical weapons.
- Alignment restricted to lawful.
- Hit Die: d8

STUNNING BLOW: All successful attacks within the next round force the victim to save vs. Spell or be stunned. This special ability automatically modifies normal attacks; no targeting needs to be done.

FLURRY OF BLOWS: Agility and prowess are key factors that allow a master of hand-to-hand combat survive in a fight against heavily armed bandits and spell-wielding sorcerers. Trained monks are capable of engaging their opponent with extraordinary speed, making them hasted and doubling their number of attacks per round. This ability lasts for 1 turn and can not be dispelled by any external sources.

DIAMOND BODY: Experienced monk channels his inner energy to induce a restorative state that heals the wounds and protects the self. For 5 rounds, the character receives 20% resistance to physical damage, regenerates 6 Hit Points per round and acquires immunity to Level Drain, Petrification and Imprisonment.

QUIVERING PALM: The next successful attack forces the opponent to save vs. Spell or die. This special ability automatically modifies normal attacks; no targeting needs to be done.~

@5031 = ~Trap mechanism deactivated.~

@5032 = ~HUMANS: Humans are the predominant race in Faerûn. Humans rule most of the significant empires and kingdoms in the Forgotten Realms. They are the most social and tolerant of races, excepting perhaps the halflings. Humans may advance as any class and are also the only race that can dual-class. Humans may not multi-class.

Humans have the following traits:
– +15% Pick Pockets, +10% Open Locks, +5% Find Traps, +5% Stealth Strike, +5% Hide in Shadows, +5% Set Traps.~

@5033 = ~DWARVES: Dwarves are short and stocky, easily identifiable by their size and shape. They have ruddy cheeks, dark eyes, and dark hair. Dwarves tend to be dour and taciturn. They are given to hard work and care little for most humor. They enjoy beer, ale, mead, but most of all, they love gold. There are four racial divisions of dwarves within the realms: shield dwarves, gold dwarves, wild dwarves, and duergar.

Dwarves have the following traits:
– +2 bonus to Saving Throws vs. Paralysis/Poison/Death, vs. Rod/Staff/Wand, and vs. Spell, with additional bonuses based on Constitution.
– Infravision.
– +10% Pick Pockets, +10% Open Locks, +20% Find Traps, +5% Detect Illusions, +10% Set Traps.
– +1 Constitution, -1 Dexterity, -2 Charisma.~

@5034 = ~ELVES: Elves tend to be shorter and slimmer than humans. Their features are finely chiseled and delicate, and they speak in melodic tones. Elves are looked upon as being frivolous and aloof. They concern themselves with natural beauty, dancing, frolicking, and other similar pursuits. Their humor is clever, as are their songs and poetry. There are six racial divisions of elves within the realms: gold elves, moon elves, wild elves, sea elves, dark elves (drow), and winged elves (avariel).

Elves have the following traits:
– 90% resistance against charm and sleep magics.
– Infravision.
– +1 THAC0 bonus with bows, short swords, and long swords.
– +20% Pick Pockets, +15% Open Locks, +5% Find Traps, +5% Stealth Strike, +15% Hide in Shadows, +10% Detect Illusions.
– +1 Dexterity, -1 Constitution.~

@5035 = ~GNOMES: Kin to dwarves, gnomes are noticeably smaller than their distant cousins. Gnomes, as they proudly maintain, are also less rotund than dwarves. Most have dark tan or brown skin, white hair, and rather large noses. Gnomes have lively and sly senses of humor, especially for practical jokes. They have a love for nature that is only matched by their love for gems and jewelry. There are two racial divisions of gnomes within the realms: rock gnomes and deep gnomes (svirfneblin).

Gnomes have the following traits:
– +2 bonus to Saving Throws vs. Rod/Staff/Wand and vs. Spell, with additional bonuses based on Constitution.
– Infravision.
– +15% Pick Pockets, +15% Open Locks, +15% Find Traps, +5% Stealth Strike, +10% Hide in Shadows, +20% Detect Illusions, +5% Set Traps.
– +1 Intelligence, -1 Wisdom.~

@5036 = ~HALFLINGS: Halflings are short, generally plump people, very much like small humans. Their faces are round and broad and often quite florid. Their hair is typically curly, and the tops of their feet are covered with coarse hair. Overall they prefer the comforts of home to dangerous adventuring. They enjoy good living, rough humor, and homespun tales. There are three racial divisions of halflings within the realms: the hairfoot, tallfellow, and stout.

Halflings have the following traits:
– +2 bonus to Saving Throws vs. Paralysis/Poison/Death, vs. Rod/Staff/Wand, and vs. Spell, with additional bonuses based on Constitution.
– +1 THAC0 bonus with slings.
– +20% Pick Pockets, +20% Open Locks, +10% Find Traps, +20% Stealth Strike, +20% Hide in Shadows.
– +1 Dexterity, -1 Strength, -1 Wisdom.~

@5037 = ~HALF-ELVES: Half-elves are a mix of human and elven blood. They are handsome folk, with good features from each of their parent races. A half-elf has the curiosity, inventiveness, and ambition of their human ancestors and the refined senses, love of nature, and artistic tastes of their elven ancestors.

Half-elves have the following traits:
– 30% resistance against charm and sleep magics.
– Infravision.
– +25% Pick Pockets, +15% Open Locks, +5% Find Traps, +10% Stealth Strike, +10% Hide in Shadows, +5% Detect Illusions.~

@5038 = ~HALF-ORCS: Half-orcs are born from the union of human and orc parents. They are as tall as humans, but a little heavier due to their muscular builds. Their greenish pigmentation, sloping forehead, jutting jaw, prominent teeth, and coarse body hair make their lineage plain for all to see. In the lands of Amn, half-orcs are tolerated, as unlike in the north the people of Amn haven't had centuries of warfare with orc kind. Half-orcs are known for their great strength.

Half-orcs have the following traits:
– Infravision.
– +1 Strength, +1 Constitution, -2 Intelligence.
– +10% Pick Pockets, +5% Open Locks, +5% Find Traps, +5% Stealth Strike.~

@5039 = ~STALKER: Stalkers serve as covert intelligence-gatherers, comfortable in both wilderness and urban settings. They are the spies, informants, and interrogators, and their mastery of stealth makes them deadly opponents.

Advantages:
-  Can backstab with 2x multiplier.
-  Gains points in both Hide in Shadows and Stealth Strike on level up.
-  +20% to Hide in Shadows and Stealth Strike abilities.
-  12th level: May memorize 2 Mage spells: Haste, Protection from Normal Missiles.

Disadvantages:
-  May not wear armor heavier than studded leather.~

@5040 = ~Ice Elemental~

@5041 = ~Magma Elemental~

@5042 = ~Ooze Elemental~

@5043 = ~Smoke Elemental~

@5044 = ~Elemental energies burst from the cracks in the golem's body fusing and merging into a paraelemental.~

@5045 = ~You're tossing the coin into the air~

@5046 = ~The coin landed clover-side up.~

@5047 = ~The coin landed clover-side down.~

@5048 = ~Lloth's Minion~

@5049 = ~Through his telekinetic powers, the Mind Flayer blocks the damage.~

@5050 = ~Monster summoned by a Conjurer gains increase in power.~

@5051 = ~Immune to Remove Specific Protections effect~

@5052 = ~Attacks per Round Doubled~

@5053 = ~AVENGER: A member of a special sect within the druidic order, a Druid of this type is dedicated to fighting those who would defile nature. Avengers have combat powers the average Druid does not — additional abilities that have been earned through extensive training, rituals and communions with entities from higher planes, a process that is very physically draining and forces them to give up some of their affinity towards nature and special powers that come with it.

Advantages:
- Gains two stars in two-handed weapon mastery.
- May achieve mastery in staffs and spears.
- May achieve specialization in weapons that are allowed to the druid domain.
- Seven spells are added to <PRO_HISHER> repertoire, all the way up to the 7th level. These are listed below:

1st level: Remove Fear.
2nd level: Draw Upon Holy Might.
3rd level: Protection from Cold.
4rd level: Holy Power.
5th level: Righteous Magic.
6th level: Giant Strength.
7th level: Protection from the Elements.

- May use Combat Trance ability once per day. Gains one use at level 13 and an additional use every 6 levels thereafter.
- At 9th level, receives a special ability Conjure Clan Spirit.
- Gains a special high level ability Perform Ritual.

Disadvantages:
- May not wear armor heavier than studded leather.
- Does not receive the usual druidic immunities and bonuses.
- Does not possess the ability to shapeshift.
- Cannot become proficient in ranged weaponry and single weapon.
- Lacks the ability to cast certain powerful druidic spells.
- Cannot dual class.

COMBAT TRANCE: From the early days, Avengers are trained to enter a trance-like state of focus. This skill, similar in spirit to focused rage of a barbarian, is achieved purely through physical training and conditioning. It allows the druid to become faster and stronger in melee combat. When in a trance state, the druid gains +1 extra attack per round and +2 bonus to <PRO_HISHER> attack and damage rolls for 1 turn.

CONJURE CLAN SPIRIT: Members of the Avenger sect practice a ritual that brings them into a state of shared consciousness. As their grasp on each others' internal energy increases, the clan members gain an ability to summon forth an ancestral spirit. The spectre will possess abilities and powers of the source, but the strength depends directly on the summoner's experience. The creature will remain in the party for 60 rounds.

PERFORM RITUAL: This ability allows the Avenger to perform a secret ritual that was perfected by members of the order. It is the ultimate reason why the druid has to sacrifice his connection to the nature. When the ritual is initiated, the Avenger attains a state of etherealness, as if stepping outside the material plane. Entering such state allows the Avenger to move faster and avoid constrictive areas. Due to his partial presense in the physical world, the druid becomes harder to hit by the ordinary melee attacks. Any type of magic that affects the druid's movement has no effect on <PRO_HIMHER>. The duration of the ability equals one turn.

Abilities:
 - +5 Bonus to Armor Class
 - +1 Bonus to movement speed
 - Doubled number of attacks per round, disregarding bonuses from Improved Haste
 - Immunity to Web, Improved Web and Vortex Web
 - Immunity to Slow, Hold and Stun effects~

@5054 = ~SWASHBUCKLER: This rogue is part acrobat, part swordsman and part wit: the epitome of charm and grace.

Advantages:
- Bonus +1 to AC.
- Gains +2 bonus to armor class every 9 levels.
- Gains +1 to hit and +2 to damage every 9 levels.
- Can specialize in any melee weapon that a thief can use.
- May place 3 slots into the proficiency 'two weapon fighting style'.
- At level 14 and above, every successful melee hit will have a 10% chance to apply a random effect picked from the following pool: "Mirrored Blade" (+3 AC bonus vs. all weapon types and 5% Magic Resistance for 6 rounds with unlimited stacking), "Life Pick" (heals the swashbuckler for 15 hp).
- At level 20 and above, every successful melee hit will also have 10% chance to apply a random effect picked from the following pool: "Bloodlet" (4D10 additional Piercing damage), "Maim Target" (4D10 additional crushing damage).
- At levels 12 and 20 gains additional 1/2 attacks per round, just like warrior classes (Fighters, Rangers and Paladins) do at levels 7 and 13.
– Starts with base scores of 40% in Open Locks and Pick Pockets.

Disadvantages:
- No backstab multiplier.
- Only 20 points to distribute at level 1.
- May not use Set Snare ability.
- May not invest any points into Set Traps and Stealth Strike.
- Does not get standard Thief bonuses to Find Traps.~

@5055 = ~RISKBREAKER: Riskbreakers are masters of simultaneous speed and accuracy. They have the ability to move and attack enemies in a way that only a blurred outline of their bodies can be seen. Riskbreakers have limited access to two mage spells as innate abilities. High level Riskbreakers gain unique abilities to break the risk involved in most difficult battles. The trainings required to become a riskbreaker are very demanding and require the riskbreaker to sacrifice a portion of his health and stamina during the process. Only Humans can be Riskbreakers.

Advantages:
- +2 Bonus to save vs. Breath Weapon.
- +2 Bonus to Movement Speed.
- Makes critical hits at a roll of 17 or better (instead of the usual 20).
- Gains "Blur" every 5 levels.
- Base Armor class lowered by 2 for every 6 levels.
- Gains "Improved Haste" at level 10.
- Gains "Whirlwind Attack" at levels 16 and 22.
- Once the Riskbreaker reaches level 15, each of his successful hits will have 15% chance to apply a random effect picked from the following pool: "Hard Hit" on target (applies 10D6 +5 additional damage), "Risk Increment" on target (applies -4 penalty to AC for 2 rounds), "Avert Risk" (heals the Riskbreaker for 20 hp).
- Gains the ability "Chain Breaker Stance" at levels 17 and 23.
- Gains the innate ability "Risk Decrement" at levels 18, 24 and 30.

Disadvantages:
- Cannot wear any armor.
- Cannot wear any helmet (other than Ioun stones).
- Cannot use gauntlets and shields.
- Cannot use ranged weapons.
- Cannot specialize in two handed weapons.
- Cannot be proficient in single weapon and Two handed weapon styles.
- Receives a -2 Penalty to constitution.
- Is immune to "Spirit Armor" and "Barkskin" spells.
- Requires 12 Intelligence.
- Cannot dual class.

Chain Breaker Stance:
This ability applies the following effects to the caster for 5 rounds:
- +25% resistance to physical damage
- 25 strength
- Regenerating 12 hp per round

Risk Decrement:
When surrounded by lots of enemies and when most other warriors may fall or surrender in despair, a high level riskbreaker is more than capable to break the risk involved in the toughest situations.

Risk Decrement has the following effects:
- Heals the riskbreaker for 10HP for every enemy hit with this ability.
- Applies a massive attack to all enemies around the riskbreaker inflicting 8D10 crushing damage with no saving throw.
- Has a good chance to throw back all or some of the enemies.
- Does not work on enemies under Protection From Magical Weapons or Absolute Immunity.~

@5056 = ~VAGRANT: Vagrants do not stay in a place for long. They spend most of their time exploring new wilderness areas and enjoying the beauties of nature. Woodlands and lakes are the most favorite places for vagrants. They are very healthy characters with exceptional stamina. Vagrants can develop a special kind of friendship with swanmays. Swanmays are very rare and special kind of lycanthrope rangers living at lakesides in woodlands and in remote temperate wetlands. High level vagrants can call for swanmays' help.

Advantages:

+1 bonus to Constitution
Immunity to disease and poison
+2 bonus to save vs. Paralyze/Death
+25% resistance to elemental damage at level 6, +15% at level 12 and +5% at level 18
Can gain grand mastery in using axes
Gains the ability to summon Swanmay at levels 13 and 16
At level 19 can summon Swanmay and Greater Swanmay, at level 12 can summon two Greater Swanmays
From level 25 can summon Swanmay Queen and Greater Swanmay
The swanmays will loyally fight at the vagrant's side for 50 rounds.

Disadvantages:

May not wear armor greater than studded leather
Cannot specialize in ranged weapons
Requires 12 Charisma
Cannot dual class~

@5057 = ~10 Stoneskins~

@5058 = ~9 Stoneskins~

@5059 = ~8 Stoneskins~

@5060 = ~7 Stoneskins~

@5061 = ~6 Stoneskins~

@5062 = ~5 Stoneskins~

@5063 = ~4 Stoneskins~

@5064 = ~3 Stoneskins~

@5065 = ~2 Stoneskins~

@5066 = ~1 Stoneskins~

@5067 = ~Check number of Stoneskins~

@5068 = ~PRIESTESS OF LLOTH:
Lloth is the chaotic evil goddess of spiders, deception, and ruthless ambition, revered by the drow of the Underdark. Her priestesses are feared and respected, weaving webs of manipulation and striking down heretics with venomous fury. Their divine magic draws on the cruel and capricious will of their goddess.

Advantages:
– From level 20, Armor of Faith cast by this kit grants 15% resistances, lasts for 50% longer, and becomes undispellable.
- Gains access to 1 new spell of level 2 - Web, 1 new spell of level 4 - Acid Shield, 1 new spell of level 5 - Protective Chant, 1 new spell of level 6 - Life Link and 1 of level 7 - Spare the Dying.
- Is immune to poison damage and poison effects.
- Gains 25% resistance to acid.
- Is completely immune to all forms of Web effects.
- Is under permanent effect of Lloth's Blessing, which grants 20% resistance to physical damage for 5 rounds to all nearby Drow and is reapplied every 5 rounds.
- From level 15 can use Aegis of Faith ability.

AEGIS OF FAITH: Through prayer and devotion, the cleric grants themselves a protective blessing that safeguards their magical defenses. For the next turn, any effects that targets and removes specific protections will be nullified. This spell does not protect against spells and effects that dispel all types of effects at once, like Remove Magic or Purge Magic.

Disadvantages:
– Alignment restricted to chaotic evil, neutral evil~

@5069 = ~Truly Horrid Umber Hulk~

@5070 = ~PRIEST OF BLIBDOOLPOOLP:
Blibdoolpoolp, the Sea Mother, is a bizarre and alien goddess worshipped by the kuo-toa - a deity of madness, ritual sacrifice, and unknowable power. Her priests draw divine strength from her twisted will, embracing visions and magics that defy mortal understanding. Though primarily clerics, they are granted limited access to druidic spells, reflecting the unnatural fusion of divine insight and primal chaos that shapes their faith.

Advantages:
- Can choose Fighter/Priest of Blibdoolpoolp multiclass option
- Gains access to Spiritual Weapon, Acid Shield, Iron Skins, Smashing Wave, Nature's Beauty and Creeping Doom
- Can cast one more spell per level
- Gains +1 bonus to casting speed
- Can use all weapons favored by kuo-toa
- Can pick Natural Restoral HLA 3 times
- From level 15 can use Aegis of Faith ability.

AEGIS OF FAITH: Through prayer and devotion, the cleric grants themselves a protective blessing that safeguards their magical defenses. For the next turn, any effects that targets and removes specific protections will be nullified. This spell does not protect against spells and effects that dispel all types of effects at once, like Remove Magic or Purge Magic.

Disadvantages:
- Alignment restricted to neutral evil
- Has no access to Summon Deva/Archdeva spells
- Has no access to Lesser Restoration, Greater Restoration and Divine Intervention spells
- Can't cast spells related to fire
- Can't use Turn Paladin/Control Undead ability~

@5071 = ~Blibdoolpoolp Battlepriest~

@5072 = ~ILLUSIONIST: A Mage who specializes in creating illusions to confuse and mislead.

Advantages:
– May cast one additional spell per level.
– Receives a +15% bonus when scribing scrolls from the Illusion school.
– Receives a +2 bonus when making Saving Throws against spells from the Illusion school.
– Targets suffer a -2 penalty when making Saving Throws against spells from the Illusion school.
- Mirror Image spell cast by Illusionist creates 5 additional images.
- When the Illusionist reaches level 15, all his spells that grant invisibility or improved invisibily apply additional Non-Detection spell to all targets.
- At level 16 Illusionists gain Simulacrum special ability.

SIMULACRUM:
This spell creates a duplicate of the caster, which closely resembles the original and acts as a powerful ally. The clone can be controlled freely and can cast spells just like the caster, it will serve the caster for 2 turns. The clone cannot engage in physical combat or use weapons. The spell does not replicate any items the caster is using or wearing. It is created at 60% of the caster's level and can cast spells of up to 3rd level 

Disadvantages:
– May not learn or cast any spells of the Necromancy school.
– Receives a -15% penalty when scribing scrolls from other schools.
- Cannot dual class.

Requires at least 16 Dexterity.~

@5073 = ~ABJURER: A Mage who specializes in protective magics.

Advantages:
– May cast one additional spell per level.
– Receives a +15% bonus when scribing scrolls from the Abjuration school.
– Receives a +2 bonus when making Saving Throws against spells from the Abjuration school.
– Targets suffer a -2 penalty when making Saving Throws against spells from the Abjuration school.
- Casts all arcane spells as if 1 level higher.
- At levels 12, 18 and 24, 30 and 36 Abjurers get Abjuration Mastery ability.

ABJURATION MASTERY: With this power a skilled Abjurers can cast any spell of their favored school bypassing the need to cleanse their aura. The chosen spell is uninterruptible and does not need to be prepared in advance. This grants Abjurers an unparalleled edge in battle, allowing them to summon protective and dispelling magic at a moment's notice.

The potency of this ability grows with the caster's experience:

At level 12: Cast spells up to 4th level
At level 14: Cast spells up to 5th level
At level 16: Cast spells up to 6th level
At level 18: Cast spells up to 7th level
At level 20: Cast spells up to 8th level
At level 22 and above: Cast any mage abjuration spell

Disadvantages:
– May not learn or cast any spells of the Alteration school.
– Receives a -15% penalty when scribing scrolls from other schools.
- Cannot dual class.

Requires at least 15 Wisdom.~

@5074 = ~CONJURER: A Mage who specializes in creating creatures and objects to assist <PRO_HIMHER>.

Advantages:
– May cast one additional spell per level.
– Receives a +15% bonus when scribing scrolls from the Conjuration school.
– Receives a +2 bonus when making Saving Throws against spells from the Conjuration school.
– Targets suffer a -2 penalty when making Saving Throws against spells from the Conjuration school.
- Maximum limit of creatures summoned at the same time is 6, not 5 when determining if a creature can be summoned by a conjuration spell cast by Conjurer.
- All creatures, apart from Elementals, Nishruu and Hakeashar, summoned by conjuration spells gain additional +2 damage, thac0, AC, strength and have 20% more hit points.
- Creatures summoned by Conjurers via Monster Summoning IV-VII spells gain additional +2 movement speed and +1 attack per round.
- From level 24, all creatures, apart from Nishruu and Hakeashar, summoned by conjuration spells become immune to spells and effects that would unsummon them. 

Disadvantages:
– May not learn or cast any spells of the Divination school.
– Receives a -15% penalty when scribing scrolls from other schools.
- Cannot dual class.

Requires at least 15 Constitution.~

@5075 = ~DIVINER: A Mage who specializes in detection and divining magics.

Advantages:
– May cast one additional spell per level.
– Receives a +15% bonus when scribing scrolls from the Divination school.
– Receives a +2 bonus when making Saving Throws against spells from the Divination school.
– Targets suffer a -2 penalty when making Saving Throws against spells from the Divination school.
- Diviners automatically learn Foreknowledge spell at level 16 without the need to scribing it into their spellbook.
- Has access to a unique High Level Ability called See Invisible.
- At levels 1, 8, and every 8 levels thereafter gains one use of Glimpse of the Future ability.

GLIMPSE OF THE FUTURE: This ability targets any single friendly creature without requiring the caster's aura to be cleansed. It sends visions of numerous potential futures to the target, providing insight on how to avoid or mitigate impending danger. The target gains a +20 bonus to all saving throws and armor class for 2 seconds.

Disadvantages:
– May not learn or cast any spells of the Conjuration school.
– Receives a -15% penalty when scribing scrolls from other schools.
- Cannot dual class.

Requires at least 16 Wisdom.~

@5076 = ~ENCHANTER: A Mage who specializes in manipulating the minds of sentient beings.

Advantages:
– May cast one additional spell per level.
– Receives a +15% bonus when scribing scrolls from the Enchantment school.
– Receives a +2 bonus when making Saving Throws against spells from the Enchantment school.
– Targets suffer a -2 penalty when making Saving Throws against spells from the Enchantment school.
- Gains an additional +1 saving throw against spells from Enchantment school every 6 levels.
- Gains one use of Focused Mind Blast ability at level 10, gains additional uses at levels 20 and 30.

FOCUSED MIND BLAST: Expertise with mind-affecting spells and creativity can make for a deadly combination. Enchanters can usurp control over enemy minds by force, or guide and join the minds of those who willingly allow them access. By casting this spell, an enchanter connects with companions from the same party and momentarily focuses on a small area within their vision. Through the enchanter's guidance, a powerful blast of cumulative telepathic energy is sent towards that point, exploding suddenly. Any creature in that area will be severely damaged, regardless of whether it has a mind or not.

The caster can achieve a similar effect alone, but the more party members join forces, the more deadly the attack will be. At level 10, the blast deals 4d6 magical damage plus an additional 2d6 for each party member. This damage increases by 2d6 for the caster and by 1d6 for party members at caster levels 16, 22, 28, 34 and 40, and it bypasses magical resistance. A party member has to be within 50 feet from the center of the spell to contribute in the damage.

- Enchanters will automatically learn a unique 4th level spell Emotion: Hope at level 7.

Disadvantages:
– May not learn or cast any spells of the Invocation school.
– Receives a -15% penalty when scribing scrolls from other schools.
- Cannot dual class.

Requires at least 16 Charisma.~

@5077 = ~INVOKER: A Mage who specializes in the manipulation of raw and elemental energies.

Advantages:
– May cast one additional spell per level.
– Receives a +15% bonus when scribing scrolls from the Invocation school.
– Receives a +2 bonus when making Saving Throws against spells from the Invocation school.
– Targets suffer a -2 penalty when making Saving Throws against spells from the Invocation school.
- Invokers learn to manipulate elemental energies better than any other arcane casters. At level 10 all elemental damage they deal will be incremented by 5%, this bonus will grow to 10% at level 20 and to 15% at level 30.
- At level 15 gains one use of Chain Sequencer, gains another use at level 25, though as with any other Sequencer, only one instance of the spell can be active at the same time.

CHAIN SEQUENCER: This is a far more dangerous form of standard Sequencer spell. The caster first chooses one spell of levels 1-3 which will be put into the sequencer and stored as an ability just like with any other Sequencer. When used, that selected spell will be cast on all non-invisible hostile creatures in a 15-ft radius from the center chosen by the caster. It is worth mentioning, that spells which require touch will have no effects.

Disadvantages:
– May not learn or cast any spells of the Enchantment school.
– Receives a -15% penalty when scribing scrolls from other schools.
- Cannot dual class.

Requires at least 16 Constitution.~

@5078 = ~TRANSMUTER: A Mage who specializes in magic that alters physical reality.

Advantages:
– May cast one additional spell per level.
– Receives a +15% bonus when scribing scrolls from the Alteration school.
– Receives a +2 bonus when making Saving Throws against spells from the Alteration school.
– Targets suffer a -2 penalty when making Saving Throws against spells from the Alteration school.
- Transmuter gains a special ability at levels 5/15/25/35, which acts just like Stoneskin, but can be cast on another character, however this version of the spell lasts for 3 turns only.
- Has access to a unique High Level Ability called Dragon Strength.
- Tenser's Transformation spell cast by Transmuters grants two pips in all weapons available to Mages, two points in Single Weapon Style and in Two-handed Weapon Style, 3/2 additional attacks per round (1 from Fighter levels and 1/2 from weapon proficiencies), Special Abilities button is also available when under the spell's effect.
- Tenser's Partial Transformation spell cast by Transmuters grants one point in Single Weapon Style and Two-handed Weapon Style and one additional attack per round.
- At level 14, 21, 28 and 35 gains one use of Blinding Speed ability.

BLINDING SPEED: This special spell makes the caster so fast, that he can traverse long distances in a blink of an eye, if there are no obstacles in his path. In addition, the number of attacks per round is doubled and this spell can't be dispelled. It lasts for 5 rounds.

Disadvantages:
– May not learn or cast any spells of the Abjuration school.
– Receives a -15% penalty when scribing scrolls from other schools.
- Cannot dual class.

Requires at least 15 Dexterity.~

